      "id": 1,
      "text": "William Locke-Paddon founded Marina on 1,500 acres he bought in 1868.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marina%2C_California"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Marina was incorporated in 1975, making it the newest city in Monterey County.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marina%2C_California"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The city’s history is tightly linked to Fort Ord, an infantry training center since the Mexican–American War.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7,
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marina%2C_California"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Every Labor Day Saturday, residents celebrate with a parade that honors the town’s military heritage.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marina%2C_California"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The 979‑acre park along the coast offers hiking, jogging, and cycling while showcasing the area’s natural and military history.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
